    "FUNC.MODE.SNGL"
  ],
  "kind": "documentation-differs",
  "title": "MODE ignores direct text and logicals instead of converting them or giving an error",
  "statement": "MODE, MODE.SNGL and MODE.MULT take only numbers from their arguments, even when text or a logical is typed directly into the call. A direct \"2\" or TRUE is not converted, so MODE(\"2\",2) and MODE(TRUE,1) are #N/A: one number, no repeat. Text that is not a number gives no error either: MODE(\"x\",2,2) is 2, and MODE(\"x\") is #N/A. Error values do come through: MODE(2,2,A3) with #DIV/0! in A3 is #DIV/0!, and of two errors the first is returned.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "30 recorded formula readings across the three functions, and 21 readings each of MODE and MODE.SNGL covering direct text, logicals and errors.",
  "inferred": null,
  "documentation": {
    "claim": "Arguments that are error values or text that can't be translated into numbers cause errors.",
    "source": "https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/office/mode-function-e45192ce-9122-4980-82ed-4bdc34973120"
  },
